.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine 1  "tine 0.8.0-beta.1" 
.SH NAME
tine \- A fast, local\-first outliner for Logseq\-compatible graphs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-capture\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIGRAPH\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fast, local\-first outliner for Logseq\-compatible graphs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the Tine version and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-capture\fR
Open Quick Capture (legacy spelling; prefer `tine capture`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIGRAPH\fR]
Graph to open in the desktop app (legacy shorthand for `tine open GRAPH`)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tine\-open(1)
Open a graph in the desktop app
.TP
tine\-capture(1)
Open Quick Capture in the desktop app
.TP
tine\-export(1)
Publish a graph as a static site or a read\-only Tine app
.TP
tine\-doctor(1)
Check that a graph can be read and parsed without changing it
.TP
tine\-version(1)
Print the Tine version and exit
.SH VERSION
v0.8.0-beta.1
